Third-party material
--------------------

runners/workerd/shellbench-worker.ts and runners/workerd/wrangler.shellbench.jsonc follow the
structure of tests/worker-backend-worker.ts and tests/wrangler.worker-backend.jsonc in
Cloudflare Computer (https://github.com/cloudflare/computer, packages/computer): the host Durable
Object that owns a Workspace whose only backend is a WorkerShellBackend dialing through the Worker
Loader binding, its __getWorkspaceStub method, the re-export of WorkspaceServiceProxy, the routing
WorkerEntrypoint, and the worker_loaders, durable_objects and migrations configuration.
runners/workerd/vitest.config.shellbench.ts follows that package's vitest configuration. These
files are meant to be copied into a cloudflare/computer checkout and import its source. Cloudflare
